From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Johnson <105193579+Johnson-Anthony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:03:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus: keep runtime cpuidle
 out of SS3

Raise domain_ss3 min-residency to 10 s on the Surface Laptop 7. s2idle
selects the system idle state by latency only (cpu_system_power_down_ok),
so suspend still enters SS3; runtime cpuidle also requires the predicted
idle time to cover the residency (cpu_power_down_ok), so it never does.
Other X1E laptops hung when the system state was entered at runtime.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
index 9f45ad930..94fd81d6e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -859,6 +859,15 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&domain_ss3 {
+	/*
+	 * s2idle picks the system state by latency alone, so suspend still
+	 * reaches SS3. Runtime cpuidle also needs the residency, which keeps
+	 * it out of SS3 while the laptop is in use.
+	 */
+	min-residency-us = <10000000>;
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
